# Devin for Terminal as a harness kiln runs in a Shards microVM: kiln plan
# 01a1ce705e4d7008993f5c7291ef4476, on the layout steps 19 to 28 share; fN are the findings of its
# research, 01a1ce705e4d70089c04cee721525c8f. kiln runs Devin as `devin acp`, its ACP server over
# stdio (Kind "devin", crates/kiln/src/harness/kinds.rs), and harness.json starts it so (f9).
#
# Cognition's own Linux bundles come in as ./devin-<arch>/: `kiln agentfiles context devin DIR`
# downloads each as pin.json pins it (its size and SHA-256 from Cognition's versioned manifest;
# Cognition publishes no signature) and unpacks it there beside harness.json, adding nothing
# (HARNESS would take an http(s) source with no checksum). It stays on its version with no setting:
# Devin's updater stayed off without the installer's `distribution` marker, which nothing here
# writes (f26). No credential is in the image: a person's sign-in lives in their HOME volume, or
# arrives through ACP's authenticate (f13).
#
#   kiln agentfiles context devin DIR --platform linux/amd64,linux/arm64
#   shards build --platform linux/amd64,linux/arm64 DIR

# Any base will do, so a project's own toolchain image works: both Linux builds are statically
# linked, with no program interpreter and no shared library, so they start on a glibc or a musl
# base alike with nothing added: no RUN, and no libc variant (f5). The default carries git, an ssh
# client, curl and CA certificates, pinned by digest as step 19 chose it.
ARG BASE=buildpack-deps:trixie-scm@sha256:4f34e1d673fdb65371de9f88bdd32c4e30152fe692b35604aef5c0b3c0e6da10
FROM ${BASE}

# BuildKit sets TARGETARCH in the global scope, so the stage declares it to name each platform's
# harness directory.
ARG TARGETARCH
HARNESS devin FROM ./devin-${TARGETARCH}

# Its network, every part named (default deny; Shards D236, destinations by name): a network for this
# harness alone, which it joins with no flow to any member, and TCP out to the hosts below alone, by
# name, through the network's boundary (--egress) and the microVM's (EXPOSE ... AS egress). Each name
# resolves for it through the agents' resolver, and no other does. Nothing comes in; no other host,
# port or protocol goes out (kiln plan 01a1cd8e862e7169a074db3d5fa33f3d, step 18:
# docs/research/s18-host-in-vm says where each host comes from).
# - server.codeium.com: Devin's API server for a Windsurf account, the default its build names
#   (WINDSURF_API_SERVER_URL moves it); api.devin.ai: the same for a devin.ai account;
#   unleash.codeium.com: its feature flags, asked as it starts (f14). Its error reports (Sentry), its
#   updater's manifests (static.devin.ai, static.windsurf.com; no updater in this layout, f26), its
#   sign-in page (app.devin.ai, in the person's browser) and `devin ssh` go nowhere.
# - host.docker.internal:7070: kiln's MCP at /api/mcp on the machine itself, at kiln's own port (its
#   http_addr's default, 0.0.0.0:7070). A kiln on another port isn't reached: the image doesn't
#   grant it, and kiln says so as it starts the harness.
NETWORK --egress=api.devin.ai:443 --egress=server.codeium.com:443 --egress=unleash.codeium.com:443 --egress=host.docker.internal:7070 provider FOR devin
EXPOSE --harnesses=devin 443/tcp 7070/tcp AS egress FOR provider
CONNECT devin WITH devin ON provider

# Its project is plugged in as it starts, at the path it has on the machine (Shards D235), so kiln
# reads its diffs, HEAD and checkpoints at that same path, and no volume holds it. Its HOME is the
# person's volume, whole: harness.json sets HOME=/home/devin, kiln's one rule for every harness it
# ships (step 18). A harness sees its image read-only, with its own /tmp scratch, so a HOME that is
# writable and kept from run to run is a volume, and what the programs it runs keep in a home (a
# .gitconfig, a tool's sign-in) is kept with it. Devin keeps its config (config.json,
# mcp_config.json) in .config/devin and its sign-in (credentials.toml), sessions and logs in
# .local/share/devin, where XDG_CONFIG_HOME and XDG_DATA_HOME point (f10, f12).
# harness.json keeps caches that follow XDG's rule on the scratch (XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/.cache),
# where they were before its HOME moved onto the volume.
# HOME in run.env needs a shards at or after 997f4e47e (v0.8.0 and later), where run.env replaces
# init's HOME=/tmp. The volume is the harness's alone, and outside /tmp, which the scratch covers.
VOLUME --target-kind=harness /home/devin FOR devin
